librepods for Debian/Ubuntu on arm64
====================================

This is upstream's Rust/iced rewrite of the LibrePods Linux client, built
from the linux-rust directory at tag linux-v0.1.0. It needs a running
BlueZ (bluetooth.service) and a desktop with a StatusNotifier tray host;
on GNOME that means an AppIndicator/KStatusNotifierItem extension.

Command line flags (see `librepods --help`):

  --debug            verbose logging (or set RUST_LOG)
  --no-tray          do not create the tray icon
  --start-minimized  start without opening the window

Per-user state lives in ~/.local/share/librepods/devices.json and
~/.config/librepods/{preferences,app_settings}.json (XDG_* respected).

Known upstream quirk in 0.1.0: the window icon is loaded from a path
relative to the source tree, so the running window has no icon when
installed. The launcher icon and tray icon are unaffected.
